    <item>
      <title>C&#43;&#43; Pthread Create Member Function Solutions: Avoiding Segmentation Faults</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/c&#43;&#43;/cpp-pthread-member-function-solutions/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/c&#43;&#43;/cpp-pthread-member-function-solutions/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;c-pthread-create-member-function-solutions-avoiding-segmentation-faults&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;C++ Pthread Create Member Function Solutions: Avoiding Segmentation Faults&amp;rdquo;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How can one reliably execute a C++ class method within a separate thread started via &lt;code&gt;pthread_create&lt;/code&gt;, while correctly supplying the necessary instance context (&lt;code&gt;this&lt;/code&gt;)?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;discussion-on-threading-c-member-functions-with-pthreads&#34;&gt;Discussion on Threading C++ Member Functions with Pthreads&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The fundamental difficulty lies in the signature required by &lt;code&gt;pthread_create&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-c&#34; data-lang=&#34;c&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;pthread_create&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;pthread_t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;thread&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;pthread_attr_t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;attr,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;                   &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;start_routine) (&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;), &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;arg);&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;start_routine&lt;/code&gt; must be a C-style function pointer (&lt;code&gt;void *(*)(void *)&lt;/code&gt;), not a pointer to a C++ member function (which implicitly requires an object instance).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
